 charlie's angel  series  beyond his work in television he served  as the music director for the grammy  awards the academy awards the primetime  emmy awards the kennedy center honors  and the 1984  summer olympic ceremony in los angeles  nightcore's theme includes a saxophone  melody played by ernie watts a long time  studio musician  watts notably played saxon marvin gaye's  let's get it on and appears on the  soundtrack for the color purple  beyond night court astute fans might  have noticed parts of the theme appear  elsewhere in pop culture  including a family guy episode in which  former u.s president bill clinton plays  saxophone  befitting a long-running show with  various court cases night court has a  lot of guest stars one of them was brent  spiner who later shot to fame as  lieutenant commander data  a self-aware android curious about human  life on star trek the next generation on  night court spiner played bob wheeler  husband to june  they appear to be down on their luck  appalachians from west virginia but are  really from  yugoslavia when asked about why they  lied bob has the perfect explanation  i don't know it was just the first  exotic place that popped into my head  the pair appear in front of harry for  various mishaps including trying egg  farming with a propane-powered incubator  as christine explains in their defense  at one point the wheelers even run a  concession stand in the courthouse  but the star trek ties don't end there  john larrick cat appeared as the klingon  malts in 1984 star trek iii the search  for spock what's more during one  marathon caseload in season six  harry hears a case involving two star  trek fans who caused a disturbance at a  seminar discussing starfleet command  one dressed as jordy leforge from the  next generation and the other  dressed as mr spock from the original  series nearly come to blows  with a ladder threatening the former  with the vulcan death grip before bull  intervenes  night court's guest stars range from the  well-known like mel tormey to actors who  had not yet earned wider recognition  like dennis haysberg  some appear in just one episode during  his run on family ties and just before  back to the future michael j  fox dropped by night court as a  shoplifting runaway whose encounter with  another defendant who thinks he's santa  claus sets him on the right path  other one-episode guest stars include  terry hatcher who played dan's boss's  sexy niece  robert englund is a defendant charged  with arson who thinks aliens are among  us  fran drescher is a schizophrenic woman  whose personality changes leave dan  literally bound and gagged  and comedian elaine boosler is joy  harry's ironically named abrasive  assistant  others like spiner had recurring roles  comedian and actor gilbert gottfried  played a temporary prosecuting attorney  over three episodes in season nine  another comedian yakov smirnoff appears  in five episodes from 1984-1999  playing russian to vector yaakov  korolenko he first appears before harry  in season one  charged for stolen property and  threatening to burn down the courtroom  in spite of this harry takes a liking to  him later helping him search for his  brother as well as obtain a visa  extension for his father  although every episode is set during the  night shift night court might be best  known for several day in the life  episodes in which the regulars work  through a hefty docket on a deadline  reasons for these time crunches include  a burst pipe flooding the holding cells  and the staff racing to beat a federal  judge's ruling granting amnesty to  anyone not arraigned by midnight  one of these stories season 5's another  day in the life is one of the series  most popular episodes  its setup involves the texas millionaire  arrested for jumping in a park fountain  who offers to pay the mortgage of an  impoverished orphanage if the staff  hears his case by midnight  meanwhile dan has a bet with the other  prosecutors on who